Continuation IV supplied an executable ExactChart boundary and a finite
resource frontier. The next distinction is between two different minimization
problems. A quotient that predicts every allowed future action is canonical;
a controller minimized for one target may choose one of several incompatible
strategies and therefore need not have a unique coarsest quotient.

The recent source-uniform acquisition results in `dev` give the corresponding
stochastic boundary: one common seed and one common rule are transported to
actual sources, while source-dependent outputs and resource tails remain in the
same-source record. This volume first treats deterministic finite contracts,
then states the source-uniform kernel extension and its limits.

